In 2129, researchers discovered a relatively inexpensive method of mass\-producing oganesson. Previously an extraordinarily rare synthetic element, oganesson proved to be a remarkably effective fuel source, exhibiting both conventional and anomalous properties. This breakthrough dramatically reduced the cost of spaceflight, making large\-scale expansion beyond Earth economically viable. With this discovery, a permanent space age began in 2031.[linebreak]

Over the next two decades, advances in propulsion and orbital industry allowed humanity to further colonize Earth orbit, and extend into Lunar orbit. By 2150, there were over 150 civilian habitats in orbit around Earth and the Moon, and, in the years that followed, the surface of the Moon was populated.[linebreak]

Additionally, the anomalous properties of oganesson allowed space faring vessels to be mass\-produced on scales that were thought only possible in science fiction.[linebreak]

[speed 50]
By 2189, humanity had set their sights to terraform Mars, and,[sleep 250] on November 23rd,[sleep 250] 2261,[sleep 500] at 18:[sleep 250]50:[sleep 250]47[sleep 250] Standard [sleep 100]Sol [sleep 100]Time,[sleep 250] it was declared complete.[sleep 1000][linebreak]

Then,[sleep 650] humanity turned elsewhere.[linebreak]

